data: {"type":"data-answer","data":{"kind":"grounded","generation":"g-ab363e","paragraphs":[{"text":"When a cashier clicks **Process Payment**, the billing app sends one JSON POST to the OpenMRS backend at `/ws/rest/v1/billing/bill/{billUuid}/payment`. The backend REST sub-resource builds a `Payment` object, attaches it to the parent `Bill`, updates the bill's status (PAID or POSTED), and saves the whole `Bill` through Hibernate, which writes the new row into the `cashier_bill_payment` table. Two repositories are involved: the frontend `openmrs-esm-billing-app` (microfrontend) and the backend `openmrs-module-billing` (Java/Spring module).","citations":[]},{"text":"Here is the path end to end.","citations":[]},{"text":"```mermaid\n---\ntitle: Payment from button click to database\n---\nflowchart TD\n  click[\"Process Payment button\"] --> handler[\"handleProcessPayment builds payload\"]\n  handler --> submit[\"processBillPayment POST\"]\n  submit --> rest[\"PaymentResource save\"]\n  rest --> svc[\"BillServiceImpl saveBill\"]\n  svc --> dao[\"HibernateBillDAO saveOrUpdate\"]\n  dao --> db[\"cashier_bill_payment table\"]\n  rest --> status[\"Bill.addPayment then synchronizeBillStatus\"]\n  status --> db\n```","citations":[]},{"text":"## 1. The button in the UI","citations":[]},{"text":"The payment panel is `Payments` [1]. It renders a **Process Payment** button only when the bill is not PENDING (a PENDING bill must be finalized first) [2]. The button stays disabled until a payment method is chosen and the amount is valid [3].","citations":[1,2,3]},{"text":"Form validation is defined with a Zod schema: the method must be non-empty, the amount must be positive, and it must not exceed the amount still due (`netAmount - tenderedAmount`) [4]. The form is wired through `react-hook-form`'s `useForm` and `useWatch` [5].","citations":[4,5]},{"text":"## 2. The click handler and the request","citations":[]},{"text":"Clicking the button runs `handleProcessPayment`, which reads the watched form values and calls `processBillPayment` [6]. The payload carries the selected method as `instanceType`, the cashier-entered `amountTendered`, and the bill's `totalAmount` as `amount`:","citations":[6]},{"text":"- `instanceType` is the payment mode (for example Cash, Mobile Money) — it names the payment type attached to this payment.\n- `amountTendered` is what the cashier actually took from the patient.\n- `amount` is the bill's total.","citations":[]},{"text":"`processBillPayment` turns that into a POST to `${apiBasePath}bill/${billUuid}/payment` with `Content-Type: application/json` [7]. On success the UI shows a \"Payment processed successfully\" snackbar, resets the form, refreshes the bill via `mutate()`, and revalidates the cached patient payment status [8]. On failure it shows an error snackbar with the returned message [9].","citations":[7,8,9]},{"text":"There is also a side effect when the patient has a current visit: `updateBillVisitAttribute` posts to the visit's `pending payment` attribute to set it to `false` [10].","citations":[10]},{"text":"## 3. The REST endpoint","citations":[]},{"text":"The URL `/bill/{uuid}/payment` is served by `PaymentResource`, declared as a sub-resource of `BillResource` with path `payment` [11]. The parent resource, `BillResource`, is registered under the `/billing` namespace [12].","citations":[11,12]},{"text":"The framework deserializes the JSON body into a new `Payment` (`newDelegate` creates an empty one [13]), then applies the `@PropertySetter` methods:","citations":[13]},{"text":"- `instanceType` is resolved from its UUID to a `PaymentMode` via `PaymentModeService`, throwing `ObjectNotFoundException` if missing [14].\n- `cashier` is resolved to a `Provider` by UUID [15].\n- `amount` and `amountTendered` are converted to `BigDecimal` [16].","citations":[14,15,16]},{"text":"`getCreatableProperties` confirms exactly which fields the client may set: `instanceType`, `attributes`, `amount`, `amountTendered`, `cashier` [17].","citations":[17]},{"text":"## 4. Save: attach the payment, sync the status","citations":[]},{"text":"The `save` method is the heart of it [18]. It:","citations":[18]},{"text":"1. If no cashier was supplied, falls back to the currently authenticated provider via `ProviderUtil.getCurrentProvider`, and throws if the logged-in user is not a provider [19].\n2. Gets the parent `Bill` already linked to the payment and calls `bill.addPayment(delegate)` [20].\n3. Calls `service.saveBill(bill)` — note it saves the **bill**, not the payment directly [21].","citations":[19,20,21]},{"text":"`Bill.addPayment` adds the payment to the bill's collection, sets the back-reference, and calls `synchronizeBillStatus()` [22].","citations":[22]},{"text":"`synchronizeBillStatus` is where the bill's state is decided [23]:","citations":[23]},{"text":"- It bails out if the bill is in a refund state (REFUND_REQUESTED, REFUNDED, PARTIALLY_REFUNDED) [24].\n- If there are payments and their total is non-zero, it compares the sum of tendered payments against the bill's amount after approved discounts [25].\n- If fully settled, the bill flips to `PAID` and all non-voided, non-refunded line items are marked `PAID` [26].\n- If not fully settled, the bill stays `POSTED` (partially paid) [27].\n- A guard `hasDiscountDrift()` keeps the bill `POSTED` for manual review if approved discounts exceed the total [28].","citations":[24,25,26,27,28]},{"text":"The totals use `getTotal()` (sum of non-voided line items) [29] and `getTotalPayments()` (sum of non-voided tendered amounts) [30].","citations":[29,30]},{"text":"## 5. Service and DAO: the actual DB write","citations":[]},{"text":"`BillServiceImpl` is an `@Transactional` service [31]. Its `saveBill` simply delegates to the DAO inside a write transaction [32].","citations":[31,32]},{"text":"`HibernateBillDAO.saveBill` calls `sessionFactory.getCurrentSession().saveOrUpdate(bill)` [33]. Because the `Bill` already exists, Hibernate updates the bill row and cascades the new `Payment` as an insert. The mapping in `Bill.hbm.xml` puts `Payment` in table `cashier_bill_payment` [34], its attributes in `cashier_bill_payment_attribute` [35], and payment modes in `cashier_payment_mode` [36].","citations":[33,34,35,36]},{"text":"## What I could not verify","citations":[]},{"text":"- I did not read the wrapper class `PaymentResource`'s exact HTTP route annotation resolution beyond the `@SubResource` declaration, nor the OpenMRS webservices framework internals that call `save`.\n- I did not confirm the exact `apiBasePath` constant value in the frontend (`constants.ts`), so the literal prefix of the REST URL is inferred from the endpoint naming.\n- The `Payment` model's own Hibernate/Hibernate mapping is inside the shared `Bill.hbm.xml`; I cited the class-level mapping but did not read every column of the `cashier_bill_payment` block.\n</answer>","citations":[]}],"gaps":[],"partialReasons":[],"abstention":null,"suggestions":[]}}

